---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="API Documentation - Rabiah Khanum">
  <div class="min-h-screen bg-gradient-to-br from-slate-50 via-white to-teal-50">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-16 sm:py-20">

      <!-- Page Header -->
      <div class="mb-5 sm:mb-6">
        <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4 leading-tight" style="font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;">
          IoT Device Management API
        </h1>
        <p class="text-base sm:text-md text-slate-600 max-w-6xl leading-relaxed">
          A REST API reference for registering and managing embedded IoT devices, with live, testable endpoints and a structure based on Postman's API documentation best practices.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mt-5">
          <span class="px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium bg-teal-100 text-teal-700 rounded-full">REST API</span>
          <span class="px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium bg-blue-100 text-blue-700 rounded-full">JSON</span>
          <span class="px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium bg-amber-100 text-amber-700 rounded-full">Live Testable</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Sample notice banner -->
      <div class="mb-5 flex items-start gap-3 bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 rounded-xl p-4 text-sm">
        <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-amber-500 flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 20 20"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M8.257 3.099c.765-1.36 2.722-1.36 3.486 0l5.58 9.92c.75 1.334-.213 2.98-1.742 2.98H4.42c-1.53 0-2.493-1.646-1.743-2.98l5.58-9.92zM11 13a1 1 0 11-2 0 1 1 0 012 0zm-1-8a1 1 0 00-1 1v3a1 1 0 002 0V6a1 1 0 00-1-1z" clip-rule="evenodd"></path></svg>
        <p class="text-amber-800 leading-relaxed">
          <strong>This is a portfolio documentation sample.</strong> The IoT Device Management API is fictional and exists to demonstrate REST API documentation skills. The base URL will not resolve. The "Try it" demos use <a href="https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com" target="_blank" class="underline font-medium">JSONPlaceholder</a> as a live mock backend so all responses are real HTTP calls.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-8">

        <!-- Sidebar nav -->
        <aside class="lg:col-span-1">
          <div class="sticky top-6 bg-white rounded-xl border border-slate-200 overflow-hidden shadow-sm">
            <div class="px-4 py-3 bg-gradient-to-r from-teal-500 to-teal-600">
              <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-white uppercase tracking-wider">On This Page</p>
            </div>
            <nav class="p-3 space-y-0.5 text-sm">
              <a href="#introduction" class="nav-link flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-slate-700 hover:bg-teal-50 hover:text-teal-700 transition-colors">Introduction</a>
              <a href="#getting-started" class="nav-link flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-slate-700 hover:bg-teal-50 hover:text-teal-700 transition-colors">Getting Started</a>
              <a href="#authentication" class="nav-link flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-slate-700 hover:bg-teal-50 hover:text-teal-700 transition-colors">Authentication</a>
              <p class="px-3 pt-3 pb-1 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-400 uppercase tracking-wider">Devices</p>
              <a href="#get-devices" class="nav-link flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-slate-700 hover:bg-teal-50 hover:text-teal-700 transition-colors">
                <span class="text-xs font-bold text-emerald-600 font-mono">GET</span> List Devices
              </a>
              <a href="#get-device-id" class="nav-link flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-slate-700 hover:bg-teal-50 hover:text-teal-700 transition-colors">
                <span class="text-xs font-bold text-emerald-600 font-mono">GET</span> Get Device
              </a>
              <a href="#post-device" class="nav-link flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-slate-700 hover:bg-teal-50 hover:text-teal-700 transition-colors">
                <span class="text-xs font-bold text-blue-600 font-mono">POST</span> Register Device
              </a>
              <p class="px-3 pt-3 pb-1 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-400 uppercase tracking-wider">Reference</p>
              <a href="#errors" class="nav-link flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-slate-700 hover:bg-teal-50 hover:text-teal-700 transition-colors">Error Codes</a>
              <a href="#toolchain" class="nav-link flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-slate-700 hover:bg-teal-50 hover:text-teal-700 transition-colors">Toolchain</a>
            </nav>
          </div>
        </aside>

        <!-- Main content -->
        <main class="lg:col-span-3 space-y-10">

          <!-- 1. Introduction -->
          <section id="introduction" class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 shadow-sm overflow-hidden">
            <div class="px-6 py-5 border-b border-slate-100">
              <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900" style="font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;">Introduction</h2>
            </div>
            <div class="px-6 py-6 space-y-5 text-slate-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
              <p>
                The <strong>IoT Device Management API</strong> lets firmware engineers and platform teams register, query, and monitor embedded devices deployed in the field. It is designed for teams managing fleets of ESP32, STM32, or other ARM Cortex-M microcontrollers that report telemetry to a central backend.
              </p>
              <p>
                Use this API to bring a new device online, retrieve its current status, or list all devices in your project by filter. It follows REST conventions: resources are nouns, actions are HTTP methods, and every response is JSON.
              </p>
              <div class="bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 rounded-xl p-5">
                <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-slate-500 uppercase tracking-wider mb-3">What you can build with this API</p>
                <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-slate-700">
                  <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                    <span class="text-teal-500 mt-0.5">&#8594;</span>
                    <span>A fleet dashboard that shows all online devices and their firmware versions in real time</span>
                  </li>
                  <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                    <span class="text-teal-500 mt-0.5">&#8594;</span>
                    <span>An onboarding script that registers new devices automatically after physical provisioning</span>
                  </li>
                  <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                    <span class="text-teal-500 mt-0.5">&#8594;</span>
                    <span>An alerting system that polls device status and flags units that have gone offline</span>
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4">
                <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl p-4 border border-slate-200">
                  <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-slate-500 uppercase tracking-wider mb-1">Base URL</p>
                  <code class="text-xs font-mono text-teal-700">api.iotfleet.example.com/v1</code>
                </div>
                <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl p-4 border border-slate-200">
                  <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-slate-500 uppercase tracking-wider mb-1">Protocol</p>
                  <p class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-800">HTTPS only</p>
                </div>
                <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl p-4 border border-slate-200">
                  <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-slate-500 uppercase tracking-wider mb-1">Response Format</p>
                  <p class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-800">JSON</p>
                </div>
                <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl p-4 border border-slate-200">
                  <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-slate-500 uppercase tracking-wider mb-1">Rate Limit</p>
                  <p class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-800">1,000 req / hour</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- 2. Getting Started -->
          <section id="getting-started" class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 shadow-sm overflow-hidden">
            <div class="px-6 py-5 border-b border-slate-100">
              <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900" style="font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;">Getting Started</h2>
            </div>
            <div class="px-6 py-6 space-y-5 text-slate-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
              <p>Follow these steps to make your first successful API call. You should be able to retrieve a list of devices within five minutes of getting your token.</p>
              <ol class="space-y-4">
                <li class="flex gap-4">
                  <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-teal-600 text-white text-xs font-bold flex items-center justify-center">1</span>
                  <div>
                    <p class="font-semibold text-slate-800 mb-1">Create an account and generate an API token</p>
                    <p class="text-slate-600">Sign in to the IotFleet dashboard, navigate to <strong>Settings &rarr; API Tokens</strong>, and create a new token scoped to your project. Copy the token. It will not be shown again.</p>
                  </div>
                </li>
                <li class="flex gap-4">
                  <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-teal-600 text-white text-xs font-bold flex items-center justify-center">2</span>
                  <div>
                    <p class="font-semibold text-slate-800 mb-1">Make your first request</p>
                    <p class="text-slate-600 mb-3">Run the following command, replacing <code class="bg-slate-100 px-1 rounded font-mono">YOUR_API_TOKEN</code> with the token you just generated. A successful response returns a <code class="bg-slate-100 px-1 rounded font-mono">200 OK</code> with a JSON list of devices.</p>
                    <!-- slim single-bar code block -->
                    <div class="bg-slate-900 rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
                      <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-3 py-1.5 bg-slate-800">
                        <span class="text-xs text-slate-400 font-mono">curl</span>
                        <button class="copy-btn-icon p-1 rounded text-slate-400 hover:text-white transition-colors" data-target="quickstart-curl" title="Copy">
                          <svg class="copy-icon w-3.5 h-3.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M8 16H6a2 2 0 01-2-2V6a2 2 0 012-2h8a2 2 0 012 2v2m-6 12h8a2 2 0 002-2v-8a2 2 0 00-2-2h-8a2 2 0 00-2 2v8a2 2 0 002 2z"/></svg>
                          <svg class="check-icon w-3.5 h-3.5 hidden text-teal-400" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2.5" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>
                        </button>
                      </div>
                      <pre id="quickstart-curl" class="px-4 py-3 text-sm font-mono text-slate-100 overflow-x-auto"><span class="text-teal-400">curl</span> -X GET <span class="text-yellow-300">"https://api.iotfleet.example.com/v1/devices"</span> \
  -H <span class="text-yellow-300">"Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_TOKEN"</span></pre>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </li>
                <li class="flex gap-4">
                  <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-teal-600 text-white text-xs font-bold flex items-center justify-center">3</span>
                  <div>
                    <p class="font-semibold text-slate-800 mb-1">Register your first device</p>
                    <p class="text-slate-600">Once you can list devices, use the <a href="#post-device" class="text-teal-600 underline">Register Device</a> endpoint to add your first ESP32 or STM32 unit to the fleet. From there, the <a href="#get-device-id" class="text-teal-600 underline">Get Device</a> endpoint lets you inspect its status and configuration at any time.</p>
                  </div>
                </li>
              </ol>
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- 3. Authentication -->
          <section id="authentication" class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 shadow-sm overflow-hidden">
            <div class="px-6 py-5 border-b border-slate-100">
              <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900" style="font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;">Authentication</h2>
            </div>
            <div class="px-6 py-6 space-y-4 text-slate-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
              <!-- point 4: rephrased the 401 sentence, removed em-dash -->
              <p>
                Every request must include a <strong>Bearer token</strong> in the <code class="font-mono bg-slate-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-slate-800">Authorization</code> header. Tokens are project-scoped and expire after 90 days. This API has no public access. Any request sent without a valid token will receive a <code class="font-mono bg-slate-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-slate-800">401 Unauthorized</code> response.
              </p>
              <div class="bg-slate-900 rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
                <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-3 py-1.5 bg-slate-800">
                  <span class="text-xs text-slate-400 font-mono">Required header on every request</span>
                  <button class="copy-btn-icon p-1 rounded text-slate-400 hover:text-white transition-colors" data-target="auth-example" title="Copy">
                    <svg class="copy-icon w-3.5 h-3.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M8 16H6a2 2 0 01-2-2V6a2 2 0 012-2h8a2 2 0 012 2v2m-6 12h8a2 2 0 002-2v-8a2 2 0 00-2-2h-8a2 2 0 00-2 2v8a2 2 0 002 2z"/></svg>
                    <svg class="check-icon w-3.5 h-3.5 hidden text-teal-400" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2.5" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>
                  </button>
                </div>
                <pre id="auth-example" class="px-4 py-3 text-sm font-mono text-slate-100 overflow-x-auto"><span class="text-slate-400">Authorization:</span> <span class="text-teal-400">Bearer YOUR_API_TOKEN</span></pre>
              </div>
              <div class="border border-slate-200 rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
                <table class="w-full text-xs">
                  <thead class="bg-slate-50">
                    <tr>
                      <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-slate-600">Property</th>
                      <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-slate-600">Value</th>
                    </tr>
                  </thead>
                  <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-100">
                    <tr>
                      <td class="px-4 py-3 text-slate-700">Auth scheme</td>
                      <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-slate-800">Bearer token</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td class="px-4 py-3 text-slate-700">Header name</td>
                      <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-slate-800">Authorization</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td class="px-4 py-3 text-slate-700">Token scope</td>
                      <td class="px-4 py-3 text-slate-600">Per project</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td class="px-4 py-3 text-slate-700">Token expiry</td>
                      <td class="px-4 py-3 text-slate-600">90 days</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td class="px-4 py-3 text-slate-700">Where to generate</td>
                      <td class="px-4 py-3 text-slate-600">Dashboard &rarr; Settings &rarr; API Tokens</td>
                    </tr>
                  </tbody>
                </table>
              </div>
              <div class="flex items-start gap-3 bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 rounded-xl p-4">
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-amber-500 flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 20 20"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M8.257 3.099c.765-1.36 2.722-1.36 3.486 0l5.58 9.92c.75 1.334-.213 2.98-1.742 2.98H4.42c-1.53 0-2.493-1.646-1.743-2.98l5.58-9.92zM11 13a1 1 0 11-2 0 1 1 0 012 0zm-1-8a1 1 0 00-1 1v3a1 1 0 002 0V6a1 1 0 00-1-1z" clip-rule="evenodd"></path></svg>
                <p class="text-sm text-amber-800">Never embed your API token in client-side code or commit it to version control. Store it in an environment variable and reference it at runtime.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- Devices divider -->
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3 pt-2">
            <span class="text-xs font-semibold text-slate-400 uppercase tracking-widest">Devices</span>
            <div class="flex-1 h-px bg-slate-200"></div>
          </div>

          <!-- 4. GET /devices -->
          <section id="get-devices" class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 shadow-sm overflow-hidden">
            <div class="px-6 py-5 border-b border-slate-100 flex items-center gap-3 flex-wrap">
              <span class="px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-bold rounded-lg bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-700 font-mono">GET</span>
              <code class="text-sm font-mono text-slate-700">/devices</code>
              <span class="ml-auto text-xs text-slate-500 italic">List all registered devices</span>
            </div>
            <div class="px-6 py-6 space-y-6 text-sm">
              <div class="space-y-2 text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
                <p>Returns a paginated list of all devices registered in your project. Use this endpoint to build dashboards, run status checks, or identify devices that need a firmware update.</p>
                <p>Results are ordered by registration date, newest first. Use the <code class="bg-slate-100 px-1 rounded font-mono">status</code> filter to narrow results to devices that are currently <code class="bg-slate-100 px-1 rounded font-mono">online</code>, <code class="bg-slate-100 px-1 rounded font-mono">offline</code>, or in an <code class="bg-slate-100 px-1 rounded font-mono">error</code> state.</p>
              </div>

              <div>
                <h4 class="font-semibold text-slate-800 mb-3">Query Parameters</h4>
                <div class="border border-slate-200 rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
                  <table class="w-full text-xs">
                    <thead class="bg-slate-50">
                      <tr>
                        <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-slate-600">Parameter</th>
                        <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-slate-600">Type</th>
                        <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-slate-600">Required</th>
                        <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-slate-600">Description</th>
                      </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-100">
                      <tr>
                        <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-slate-800">status</td>
                        <td class="px-4 py-3 text-slate-600">string</td>
                        <td class="px-4 py-3 text-slate-500">No</td>
                        <td class="px-4 py-3 text-slate-600">Filter by device status. Accepted values: <code class="bg-slate-100 px-1 rounded">online</code>, <code class="bg-slate-100 px-1 rounded">offline</code>, <code class="bg-slate-100 px-1 rounded">error</code>. Omit to return all devices.</td>
                      </tr>
                      <tr>
                        <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-slate-800">limit</td>
                        <td class="px-4 py-3 text-slate-600">integer</td>
                        <td class="px-4 py-3 text-slate-500">No</td>
                        <td class="px-4 py-3 text-slate-600">Number of results per page. Default: <code class="bg-slate-100 px-1 rounded">20</code>. Maximum: <code class="bg-slate-100 px-1 rounded">100</code>.</td>
                      </tr>
                      <tr>
                        <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-slate-800">page</td>
                        <td class="px-4 py-3 text-slate-600">integer</td>
                        <td class="px-4 py-3 text-slate-500">No</td>
                        <td class="px-4 py-3 text-slate-600">Page number for pagination. Starts at <code class="bg-slate-100 px-1 rounded">1</code>. Use alongside <code class="bg-slate-100 px-1 rounded">limit</code> to page through large fleets.</td>
                      </tr>
                    </tbody>
                  </table>
                </div>
              </div>

              <!-- point 6: slim single bar with lang label + copy icon together -->
              <div>
                <h4 class="font-semibold text-slate-800 mb-3">Request Example</h4>
                <div class="rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-slate-800">
                  <div class="flex items-center bg-slate-800 px-3 py-1.5 gap-3">
                    <button class="tab-btn active-tab text-xs font-medium text-white px-2 py-1 rounded" data-tab="get-devices-curl">curl</button>
                    <button class="tab-btn text-xs font-medium text-slate-400 hover:text-white transition-colors px-2 py-1 rounded" data-tab="get-devices-js">JavaScript</button>
                    <div class="ml-auto">
                      <button class="copy-btn-icon p-1 rounded text-slate-400 hover:text-white transition-colors" data-target="get-devices-curl-code" title="Copy">
                        <svg class="copy-icon w-3.5 h-3.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M8 16H6a2 2 0 01-2-2V6a2 2 0 012-2h8a2 2 0 012 2v2m-6 12h8a2 2 0 002-2v-8a2 2 0 00-2-2h-8a2 2 0 00-2 2v8a2 2 0 002 2z"/></svg>
                        <svg class="check-icon w-3.5 h-3.5 hidden text-teal-400" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2.5" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>
                      </button>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  <div id="get-devices-curl" class="tab-panel bg-slate-900">
                    <pre id="get-devices-curl-code" class="px-4 py-3 text-sm font-mono text-slate-100 overflow-x-auto"><span class="text-teal-400">curl</span> -X GET <span class="text-yellow-300">"https://api.iotfleet.example.com/v1/devices?status=online&limit=10"</span> \
  -H <span class="text-yellow-300">"Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_TOKEN"</span> \
  -H <span class="text-yellow-300">"Content-Type: application/json"</span></pre>
                  </div>
                  <div id="get-devices-js" class="tab-panel hidden bg-slate-900">
                    <pre id="get-devices-js-code" class="px-4 py-3 text-sm font-mono text-slate-100 overflow-x-auto"><span class="text-blue-400">const</span> response = <span class="text-blue-400">await</span> fetch(
  <span class="text-yellow-300">"https://api.iotfleet.example.com/v1/devices?status=online&limit=10"</span>,
  &#123;
    method: <span class="text-yellow-300">"GET"</span>,
    headers: &#123;
      <span class="text-yellow-300">"Authorization"</span>: <span class="text-yellow-300">`Bearer $&#123;apiToken&#125;`</span>,
      <span class="text-yellow-300">"Content-Type"</span>: <span class="text-yellow-300">"application/json"</span>
    &#125;
  &#125;
);
<span class="text-blue-400">const</span> data = <span class="text-blue-400">await</span> response.json();</pre>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div>
                <h4 class="font-semibold text-slate-800 mb-1">Response Example</h4>
                <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 mb-3">200 OK · Three online devices returned, newest first</p>
                <div class="bg-slate-900 rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
                  <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-3 py-1.5 bg-slate-800">
                    <span class="text-xs text-slate-400 font-mono">json</span>
                    <button class="copy-btn-icon p-1 rounded text-slate-400 hover:text-white transition-colors" data-target="get-devices-response" title="Copy">
